== Notes ==
* {{Dlc|r}} C.H.A.D is much less common than his counterpart, spawning only 1/4th as often.
* C.H.A.D can spawn alongside 2 {{e|Boil}}s or 2 {{e|Red Boom Fly|text=Red Boom Flies}}.
* Each segment of C.H.A.D. can be individually damaged, so a single piercing tear could hit C.H.A.D. multiple times.
** {{Dlc|r}} Piercing shots no longer damage segmented enemies multiple times per attack.

== Trivia ==
* C.H.A.D. appeared in the original ''The Binding of Isaac''.
* He is a rare alternative to {{e|Chub}}.
* C.H.A.D. is a cameo from ''Super Meat Boy'', a game by Edmund McMillen.
** In ''Super Meat Boy'', he is the boss of Chapter 2: The Hospital.
** When defeated in Super Meat Boy, C.H.A.D. would shrink to a smaller version of himself. Him getting smaller during the fight in ''Rebirth'' and the item {{i|Little C.H.A.D.}} are allusions to this.
* The name C.H.A.D. is a reference to the 1984 horror film ''[[wikipedia: C.H.U.D.|C.H.U.D.]]'', [http://new.spring.me/#!/EdmundM/q/400190223683714377 confirmed by Edmund].
* Despite C.H.A.D. normally being speculated to stand for "Cute, Huge and Deadly," Edmund McMillen had confirmed that [https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1102940262400090112 it doesn't stand for that phrase].
** When asked what it does stand for, Edmund jokingly replied [https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1300372521447874560 that he can't legally say].
* C.H.A.D.'s secret for unlocking him says "In the {{s|Depths}}" even though he is found in The Caves.
* {{plat|PS4, Vita}} Even though C.H.A.D is unlocked by accomplishing "Something Cute", its PSN Trophy icon features Chub.

